  "history_summaries": [
    "Round 1: Fixed DUT bug in newHanoi.scala line 43. Root cause: when(legal) disc(sizeFrom) := io.to unconditionally wrote io.to without validating it's a valid peg (≤2). io.to=3 (invalid) would corrupt disc state, causing all 22 CEXs including disc_0_valid_peg, disc_{1..19}_valid_peg, done_stays_done, and legal_move_to_valid_peg. Fix: changed when(legal) to when(legal && io.to <= 2.U), preventing invalid peg values from ever being written to disc registers. This addresses the causal path — invalid inputs cannot propagate into internal state. All 20 disc_*_valid_peg assertions and legal_move_to_valid_peg assertion labels preserved unchanged.",
    "Round 2: Fixed two remaining DUT bugs in newHanoi.scala. (1) legal_move_to_valid_peg: The legal computation on line 43 did not require io.to <= 2.U, so io.to=3 could make sizeTo=20 (empty peg) and incorrectly classify the move as legal, violating !legal || io.to <= 2.U. Fix: added && io.to <= 2.U to legal definition, addressing the causal path — an invalid peg input cannot be classified as legal. (2) done_stays_done: After all 20 discs reach peg B, inputs io_from=B, io_to=A could still trigger a legal disc move (disc_19 B→A), breaking the solved state. Fix: added && !io.done to the when guard, preventing any move after puzzle completion. Both assertion labels (done_stays_done, legal_move_to_valid_peg) preserved exactly. No homologous assertions found."
  ],
